  clock: 4  # 0b67
  nonce: 0b67  # 0b67
  message: "Classification half fixed in PR #1616 (d1220b7bc4); parse-cost half split out as WI-lutud. Puzzle answered: lean's parser.c contributed zero nodes because it was ALREADY tier 4 by its '@generated' header -- parsed (partial parse, 31 damaged nodes), then dropped by the default tier filter (limits.tier_filtered_files on the c907 self-survey); its 305,712 lines were in the profile's LOC (now left out by WI-kojul). circom's and wolfram's parser.c carry no header and were tier 3. Fix: supply_chain._GENERATOR_FINGERPRINTS (C-family only, 4 KiB head, feeds tier and is_generated): tree-sitter (parser.h include AND #define LANGUAGE_VERSION), Bison/flex/re2c banner on a comment line, #line into .y/.yy/.ypp/.l/.ll/.lex/.rl/.re. Evidence: classify_file on the real tree -- all three vendored parser.c DERIVED/is_generated, lean scanner.c and wolfram scanner.cc stay EXTERNAL_DEP; tests TestGeneratorFingerprints (incl. negatives: hand-written scanner, banner in a string literal, fingerprint text in a .py). Analogues: corpus sweep of 158,304 C-family files in ~/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos -> 36 matches (Bison 26, flex 5, grammar #line 5: modsecurity, virtualbox, seabios, kbuild, ClickHouse rageled_files), all generator output, none previously marked. NOT done: self-survey before/after (tier-4 files are still parsed, so wall time would not move; that is WI-lutud)."  # 0b67
